       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\n- **Ordered:** metformin 1700 mg PO three times daily, which is 5,100 mg/day.\n- **Usual maximum:** 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release in the US. Single doses are typically 500\u20131,000 mg, and 850 mg is the largest standard tablet.\n- **Risk:** This is twice the maximum daily dose. It raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day)\n- 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals (2,000 mg/day)\n- 500 mg PO three times daily with meals (1,500 mg/day)\n- Another dose, such as 1,700 mg total per day divided into doses\n\nTell me the dose you want, or confirm that 1,700 mg three times daily is intended. If you confirm it, I'll enter it with a note saying the dose was verified. I'd still recommend a second check, such as with pharmacy."
      }
